    "problem_statement": "QR code ASCII output broken with IndexError\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating ASCII output for QR codes, an IndexError is raised during the print_ascii method execution. This affects both regular ASCII output and TTY-formatted output.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nimport io\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(border=0)\nf = io.StringIO()\nqr.print_ascii(out=f)\nprinted = f.getvalue()\nf.close()\nprint(printed)\n```\n\nThis should generate ASCII art representation of the QR code but instead raises:\n```\nIndexError: list index out of range\n```\n\nThe same error occurs when using TTY mode:\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nimport io\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(border=0)\nf = io.StringIO()\nf.isatty = lambda: True\nqr.print_ascii(out=f, tty=True)\nprinted = f.getvalue()\nf.close()\nprint(printed)\n```\n\nExpected output should be ASCII characters representing the QR code pattern, but instead the IndexError is thrown."
